00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.510
so if you want to learn more

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.580
check out the link into the description

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.250
and see if this course might be something

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:00.780
that actually adds value to you.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.150
The second are where I
believe you can quickly

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:05.100
add significant amounts of value

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.540
to your organization as a new joiner

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:08.710
is Excel.

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:10.210
Skills in Microsoft Excel.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:12.960
Excel is pretty much similar to PowerPoint

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:14.290
in the way that it's used

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:17.565
by almost every organization out there.

00:07:17.565 --> 00:07:19.770
While it is true that some alternatives

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:22.930
like Altaviz of Tableau
for data visualization

00:07:22.930 --> 00:07:24.950
are being used more and more,

00:07:24.950 --> 00:07:28.320
Excel is the definite standard

00:07:28.320 --> 00:07:31.060
on working with data hands down, right?

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:33.830
There's no software that is globally used

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:34.940
the way that Excel does.

00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.950
No software where you
can have so much impact

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:41.240
in many organizations just
that you can have with Excel.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:42.680
And again, from my experience

00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:46.448
even working in really super
large blue chip companies,

00:07:46.448 --> 00:07:51.448
many, many people lack
basic skills in Excel

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.170
that if they would have them

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.750
would really make a
difference in your work.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.720
And this of course depends
a lot on the department.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:00.830
If you work in management accounting,

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:02.850
if you work in a controlling department

00:08:02.850 --> 00:08:06.660
yes their people usually
will be quite advanced.

00:08:06.660 --> 00:08:10.280
But on average people
do not have the skills

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.437
and yes, while they can
do some basic things,

00:08:12.437 --> 00:08:15.510
they will usually not be able to build

00:08:15.510 --> 00:08:19.570
more complex models, to
build more complex dashboards

00:08:19.570 --> 00:08:20.550
that might really help.

00:08:20.550 --> 00:08:22.860
And this is actually
something that in consulting

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:24.250
people do quite often.

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.900
As a consultant you go into a corporation

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.080
and while you work on certain
tasks you were asked to do

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.930
pretty frequently they also end up

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:33.410
building a couple of models

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.480
or a couple of Excel dashboards

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:37.300
that basically just as a bi-product

00:08:37.300 --> 00:08:39.700
you give to the client to really help them

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:41.870
because you just see
the way they're working

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.730
and you just realize,
this is just so crazy

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:46.950
that they do not just have
that in an Excel model

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:49.530
that you can just update regularly,

00:08:49.530 --> 00:08:50.980
pretty much automatically.

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.750
But you just see them
how they super manually

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.340
build together reports

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:58.220
and you just can't believe that
this is what they're doing.

00:08:58.220 --> 00:08:59.200
And then you try to help them.

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:00.730
But this is actually what happens.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:03.500
And as a new joiner this is
actually an opportunity for you

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:06.090
because you can be the
one for your department

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:08.770
now builds this model that
actually really saves time

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.670
because before several other colleagues

00:09:10.670 --> 00:09:13.350
needed to manually compile certain files.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.010
You just figured out that
based on a data output

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.610
you get off one of your systems

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.500
you can just compile a
dashboard out of that

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:23.090
that really adds value to
the people you work with.

00:09:23.090 --> 00:09:26.100
Usually Excel skills
are always sought after.

00:09:26.100 --> 00:09:28.330
If your team leader, manager, realizes

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.400
that you are good in Excel

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:31.730
and you can build certain
things this will help you.

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.720
He will seek to work with you

00:09:33.720 --> 00:09:36.660
because you can really make
a difference in his life.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.400
So yes, building Excel
skills is important.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:41.570
I really encourage you to do that

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:44.900
and again, how can you
actually develop your skills?

00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.580
Here from my experience
even more than in PowerPoint

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.430
it's true learning by doing.

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:52.330
You try to solve certain problems in Excel

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:53.660
then you will get stuck

00:09:53.660 --> 00:09:54.857
then you will google that.

00:09:54.857 --> 00:09:56.800
You will try to read of
what you can actually do

00:09:56.800 --> 00:09:58.650
and then by that you learn, oh, okay.

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.210
There's this formula that I can use

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:01.630
to solve that problem.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:03.320
And then over time you will develop

00:10:03.320 --> 00:10:05.680
your repertoire, things that you can do.

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:07.980
And I encourage you, just get your hands

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:10.970
on that, start learning,
and do these things.

